{"timestamp": "2026-08-04T21:29:12.334809", "data": {"url": "https://www.marvel.com/comics/guides/1284/80th-anniversary-silver-age", "title": "80th Anniversary: Silver Age | Marvel Universe | Marvel Comic Reading List", "content": "MARVEL COMICS: 1961-1970 (3205) Marvel Unlimited Want to read all these digital comics? Get instant access to all these and more! Join Now Restrictions Apply. Fantastic Four In Fantastic Four (1961) #1 The series most credited for kick starting the Marvel Universe, Fantastic Four proved a commercial success in large part to its non-traditional heroes. This series also put Jack Kirby and Stan Lee on the map! Spider-Man In Amazing Fantasy (1962) #15 Readers have always resonated with high school student Peter Parker, a goodhearted kid who gains the powers of a spider. Stan Lee and Steve Ditko bring the web-slinger to life! Hulk In Incredible Hulk (1962) #1 Witness the birth of the Gamma Green Giant, as mild-mannered Bruce Banner gets a dose of radiation he can't quite shake! Ant-Man & the Wasp In Tales To Astonish (1959) #27 Creators Stan Lee, Larry Lieber, Steve Ditko, and Jack Kirby present 'The Man in the Ant Hill', the origin story of Hank Pym! Read on for his adventures with stylish sidekick, the winsome Wasp! Thor In Journey Into Mystery (1952) #83 The comic that introduced True Believers to the God of Thunder! When Dr. Donald Blake strikes his wooden cane on the ground, he transforms into Odin\u2019s favored son! Iron Man In Tales Of Suspense (1959) #39 Although he wouldn't get a solo series till 1968, Iron Man starred in Tales of Suspense, a Cold War Era comic with a sci-fi bend. In a moment of duress, industrialist Tony Stark achieves his full potential. X-Men In X-Men (1963) #1 In their inaugural issue, Charles Xavier's first class of mutants takes on Magneto, Master of Magnetism. But the X-Men\u2019s greatest threat would be a world that hates and fears their existence. Avengers In Avengers (1963) #1 The Avengers are the pinnacle Super Hero Team-Up\u2013a combination of power sets and personalities that guarantees an exciting read! Doctor Strange In Strange Tales (1951) #110 Arrogant surgeon Stephen Strange turns to the Mystic Arts following a life-altering accident. But in his first appearance, the future Sorcerer Supreme is actually a \u201cMaster of Black Magic\u201d! Daredevil In Daredevil (1964) #1 By day, he is blind attorney Matt Murdock, but in his suit of red, he is Daredevil, Man Without Fear. Check out the hero of Hell's Kitchen in his first appearance, wearing a (very) yellow costume! Black Panther In Fantastic Four (1961) #52 In the technologically advanced nation of Wakanda, the Fantastic Four cross paths with a noble king and righteous hero\u2013meet Marvel\u2019s first African super hero, Black Panther! Captain America In Captain America (1968) #100 The star-spangled Sentinel of Liberty enters the Silver Age! Having earned his place amongst modern Marvel-dom, Steve Rogers takes off in his own ongoing series!", "lists": [["Skip Menu", "", "", "", "MARVEL UNLIMITED SUBSCRIBE", ""], ["News", "Comics", "Characters", "Games", "Movies", "TV Shows", "Videos", "More"], ["", "News", "Comics", "Characters", "Games", "Movies", "TV Shows", "Videos", "Lifestyle", "Role-Playing Game", "Gear", "Books", "Podcasts", "Shop", "", "Marvel Unlimited Access Over 30,000+ Digital Comics"], ["About Marvel", "Help/FAQs", "Careers", "Internships"], ["Advertising", "Disney+", "Marvelhq.com", "Redeem Digital Comics"], ["", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""]], "tables": [], "code_blocks": [], "meta_description": "Marvel.com is the official site of Marvel Entertainment! Browse official Marvel movies, characters, comics, TV shows, videos, & more.", "meta_keywords": "", "og_image": "", "js_rendered": true, "js_message": "Page appears to be rendered by a JavaScript framework; content may be incomplete.", "success": true, "error": "", "truncated": false, "fetched_bytes": 256245, "total_bytes": 256245}}